<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-all</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:56:32Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-all" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-all" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Trump promises Americans $5,000 if Republicans win midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c6e6a4a83ce9881e76b9a6a5d236906dfd8802b1cb1a555db74d9eabd0f37c11</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:56:18Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T03:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-promises-americans-5-000-if-republicans-win-midterms/a-79208399--193518c15bf4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-promises-americans-5-000-if-republicans-win-midterms/a-79208399?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US president gave a wide-ranging speech at the Republican midterm convention. He defended the war in Iran, trade wars and tariffs, and the White House ballroom. He also called Democrats evil and immigrants animals.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Philippines: Several killed, dozens missing after fire on ferry</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a6cbd66387dd51d9e2a4a980d648fd3cc0d2b2392900229ff3de1f6928602cbb</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:56:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T01:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/philippines-several-killed-dozens-missing-after-fire-on-ferry/a-79208236--4b1ef54015f4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/philippines-several-killed-dozens-missing-after-fire-on-ferry/a-79208236?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Footage released by the Coast Guard showed the vessel engulfed in flames as rescuers brought bodies ashore in body bags. The ship's manifest listed 134 passengers and crew.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Finland: Google announces €13 billion AI, energy investment</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:baf06a67ace0325a74117d2faad35d4a9749e0eefedcc7baff0f33a81c6204a0</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:56:23Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T22:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/finland-google-announces-_13-billion-ai-energy-investment/a-79208034--066f4655241f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/finland-google-announces-€13-billion-ai-energy-investment/a-79208034?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Google has announced a plan to expand AI data centers and buy massive amounts of nuclear energy. Finland's security services have warned of there are risks, but the right-wing government says the deal will bring jobs.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Norway's PM: Zelenskyy's plane almost hit by drone</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c2e7dd309258169b0417d5fa65ebf5d594c0a31b686af59b18e4d169a94f06de</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:56:26Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T20:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/norway-s-pm-zelenskyy-s-plane-almost-hit-by-drone/a-79207528--c78d6300cd95.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/norway-s-pm-zelenskyy-s-plane-almost-hit-by-drone/a-79207528?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A drone nearly struck a plane carrying Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy from Moldova to Oslo, according to Norway's prime minister. However, a Ukrainian source said the threat may have been overstated.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>China: English to be removed as a graded core subject?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4c0ae3cf1e6d66c39f1e69d23682673d553794373f55330b78123263ab7d8ead</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:56:29Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T19:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-english-to-be-removed-as-a-graded-core-subject/a-79199629--52f7a1cb9d3e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-english-to-be-removed-as-a-graded-core-subject/a-79199629?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A university professor is calling for English to no longer be taught as a graded core subject in Chinese schools. Opponents argue that, in a globalized world, knowing English is beneficial for the country and career.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ceuta: Documents show Spanish intelligence warned of crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6f4a6ab1f589188485151b37b843c6b6c7beb6684b492c2233cbdf74aeec9d2b</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:56:32Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T17:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ceuta-documents-show-spanish-intelligence-warned-of-crisis/a-79206505--1dd65a7f978d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ceuta-documents-show-spanish-intelligence-warned-of-crisis/a-79206505?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Spain declassified documents that showed warnings issued a day before more than 70,000 migrants rushed the Ceuta border fence. Meanwhile, the EU announced funds to strengthen the border and return migrants to Morocco.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's connection to the September 11, 2001 attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:59123c65c3abf555de12edfdc3615d6398cb87cb0237b68eb0e164e27a184823</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T17:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-connection-to-the-september-11-2001-attacks/a-79202918--22a07e00351f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-connection-to-the-september-11-2001-attacks/a-79202918?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The 9/11 attacks were partly planned in Hamburg, via the so-called Hamburg cell, whose members played key roles in the plot. A look back at a day that shook up Germany’s approach to national security.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Serbia, the conflicted EU candidate</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2b11895ce754cf564aa25dc73db4d112c2162722ba15fa7069c3a4d07a65b6bf</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T16:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/serbia-the-conflicted-eu-candidate/a-79203774--0a94078faf3f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/serbia-the-conflicted-eu-candidate/a-79203774?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">On paper, Belgrade has pursued EU membership for years. But accession has long been stalled. The hero's farewell given to war criminal Mladic exposed just how far Serbia has alienated itself from Europe.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Switzerland: Two killed in power plant explosion</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:72ccb14f8b0484be37a55a094e9be94f4cf74b9a59bca49f3877effeea0f4fe7</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T16:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/switzerland-two-killed-in-power-plant-explosion/a-79205516--3f73e13d5b04.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/switzerland-two-killed-in-power-plant-explosion/a-79205516?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A fire and subsequent explosion have killed two workers at a Swiss hydroelectric power plant. Authorities say the facility suffered major damage in the incident.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Iran tightens social control with crackdown on cafes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c104e86a433e4a1e65c0f1856f1447e14dc9a3cc1852edfcb49c72155c755b08</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T15:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-tightens-social-control-with-crackdown-on-cafes/a-79204988--56f8af8e2572.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-tightens-social-control-with-crackdown-on-cafes/a-79204988?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Authorities are keeping a close eye on cafes, fearing they could play a role in fostering anti-government sentiment.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ethiopia's constitutional reform: What does it mean — especially for Abiy?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b7de0e7c723aa60e430632c19e5ef4ccc10f97b8685f8ce640a52bdac1d1dd17</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T15:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ethiopia-s-constitutional-reform-what-does-it-mean-especially-for-abiy/a-79172262--7aa1de37183a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ethiopia-s-constitutional-reform-what-does-it-mean-especially-for-abiy/a-79172262?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Does Ethiopian Prime Minister Abiy Ahmed stand to benefit from a planned constitutional reform in the country? A new presidential system would reshape political power — and could give him even more power in office.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Oil prices rise as Middle East conflict escalates</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f06c178efb9fd243d64c59ad7cd147dc70eee231812a7c300d141232e8d2f440</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T14:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/oil-prices-rise-as-middle-east-conflict-escalates/a-79203547--69f3e58c677b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/oil-prices-rise-as-middle-east-conflict-escalates/a-79203547?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The price of oil returned to triple digits in US dollars, as conflict in the Middle East threatens supply chains and puts a strain on global reserves.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Syria arms depot explosion kills at least 14</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e31f32218cc2b9ec923a7f3534f765ab1defa8a78e8ec0d2376701dd64b83fbf</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T13:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/syria-arms-depot-explosion-kills-at-least-14/a-79203314--22d7b8669d08.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/syria-arms-depot-explosion-kills-at-least-14/a-79203314?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The explosion struck near the Syrian city of Sarmada in Idlib province in the northwest. The Defense Ministry said the weapons and remnants from the war were being stored temporarily at the site before being relocated.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>How Belarusians still find hope in a silenced country</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fe04df071ec273eb7b43e99b0bec812bda101c8dd2056084942713c406ed641a</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T13:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-belarusians-still-find-hope-in-a-silenced-country/a-79127285--d234556fa838.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-belarusians-still-find-hope-in-a-silenced-country/a-79127285?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The documentary "Letters From the Silenced Country" depicts the ongoing repression under the authoritarian regime. Director Andrei Kutsila talked to DW ahead of the film's Venice premiere.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Why we're still looking for dark matter</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cf47a75ba81ba5fb71c497333717787a767b5bd25fd4f610a8f259f8d4800cfe</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T13:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-we-re-still-looking-for-dark-matter/a-79189395--3bfbe0fa2ce3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-we-re-still-looking-for-dark-matter/a-79189395?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">When physicists said they may have spotted evidence of dark matter almost 100 years after it was proposed as a theory, the internet lit up. Here's why we're searching for the thing that holds everything else together.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Cambodia's floating schools hit by rising fuel costs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d10f36a573359d22d1d8c0d49aa1a2a0970aaaa4fab9b97daa324578a0ca00a8</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T12:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cambodia-s-floating-schools-hit-by-rising-fuel-costs/a-79202008--dc2e9aeeea22.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cambodia-s-floating-schools-hit-by-rising-fuel-costs/a-79202008?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Iran war has sent fuel prices higher in Cambodia, squeezing families who rely on fishing and boats for their livelihoods. For children living on Tonle Sap, rising fuel costs pose yet another barrier to education.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>EU proposes more restrictions for Airbnb, holiday rentals</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2c535c450f7a634ab376ff8234addd64e0a6073a468199d721cc9b95cd9cf537</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T12:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-proposes-more-restrictions-for-airbnb-holiday-rentals/a-79202023--ad637f480100.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-proposes-more-restrictions-for-airbnb-holiday-rentals/a-79202023?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Union wants tighter rules on short-term rentals to tackle housing shortages in tourist hotspots.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Syria: How  the 'house of sisters' threat split society</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c921885d55a9e6b502d35317a9b76091782ab4c6333bef5b4869e2bd50767898</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T11:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/syria-how-the-house-of-sisters-threat-split-society/a-79192163--b9de2b546f7f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/syria-how-the-house-of-sisters-threat-split-society/a-79192163?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Rumor has it that the 'house of sisters' is where kidnapped women from other Syrian sects are forced to convert to Islam. Nobody knows if it really exists, but it's being used to create communal tensions anyway.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>LIV Golf in financial turmoil: what's next for the sport?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:92ea12f4014f736ba4bb80c2656c18588db9ccbfde804e6a6baef58a5c95a745</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T11:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/liv-golf-in-financial-turmoil-what-s-next-for-the-sport/a-79199569--378367d5fd0c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/liv-golf-in-financial-turmoil-what-s-next-for-the-sport/a-79199569?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Six months after Saudi Arabia pulled funding from the breakaway organization, LIV Golf have filed for bankruptcy protection. Several of the world's best players signed on to LIV, so where does that leave golf?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Norway's King Harald V laid to rest in state funeral</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:731019fd30571f4d4e8aa777d3869e090d3c9f3889fff240055c55a416570c81</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T11:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/norway-s-king-harald-v-laid-to-rest-in-state-funeral/a-79199812--18dfde6e8405.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/norway-s-king-harald-v-laid-to-rest-in-state-funeral/a-79199812?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Heads of state from around the world came to Oslo to pay tribute to the late monarch.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Conspiracy theories can provide answers but not peace</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8d98b7cd3a979365d93dd5d583c4791bcb2c2835588d11975bbe3b63590ceb8a</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T09:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/conspiracy-theories-can-provide-answers-but-not-peace/a-79022756--b464ce7f771c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/conspiracy-theories-can-provide-answers-but-not-peace/a-79022756?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Twenty-five years after 9/11, conspiracy theories about the terrorist attacks persist. But even as an attempt to make sense of a tragedy, psychologists say the benefit in conspiracy ideation or belief is short-lived.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>The billion-euro trade driving Europe's eels to extinction</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e93dc7ef565d6fcb4de6a729308b5872c2ef5f86cf218ca6b73264a001c6d725</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T08:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-billion-euro-trade-driving-europe-s-eels-to-extinction/a-78523145--e574ad564b10.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-billion-euro-trade-driving-europe-s-eels-to-extinction/a-78523145?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Traffickers are making big bucks smuggling millions of critically endangered eels across continents, using suitcases on planes and legal loopholes to deliver them to dinnerplates. Where are the smuggling hotspots?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>The Bayeux Tapestry in London: What's behind the hype?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d63e626ed513c625b72d5719a1aea43dbda95e79204dac323c0a00adc3457310</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T07:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-bayeux-tapestry-in-london-what-s-behind-the-hype/a-78488629--9a9477f8929c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-bayeux-tapestry-in-london-what-s-behind-the-hype/a-78488629?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The exhibition of the Bayeux Tapestry at the British Museum is eagerly anticipated across the UK, as the medieval masterpiece is considered by many to be a symbol of the country's identity.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>EU sports commissioner says FIFA is 'damaging to football'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ac30fa0f9046896efa9f09af15289baeb5b7d211a053bf433328152dc01578bb</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T07:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-sports-commissioner-says-fifa-is-damaging-to-football/a-79193424--c7a4bd30a298.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-sports-commissioner-says-fifa-is-damaging-to-football/a-79193424?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Speaking to DW, EU Commissioner Glenn Micallef hit out at world football's governing body over its "poor governance."</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>BRICS leaders gather in India, but does the group have a clear purpose?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0e580c44fde12d615b40bcc18d822138371b8e7404bdf02cecb0d2fb6791afa4</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T06:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/brics-leaders-gather-in-india-but-does-the-group-have-a-clear-purpose/a-79195234--96a91b3eb8a9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/brics-leaders-gather-in-india-but-does-the-group-have-a-clear-purpose/a-79195234?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The 18th BRICS summit takes place in India this weekend. Unlike last year, the leaders of China and Russia are coming. But does the expanded group have a clear common mission and purpose?</summary><category term="NRS-Import" /></entry><entry><title>Putin rejects mobilization rumors, many Russians unconvinced</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9ac8832ee7b2094ca7a76a31f7a3b024100e1e67d235c166fa10bf574fbf5704</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T05:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/putin-rejects-mobilization-rumors-many-russians-unconvinced/a-79193386--b343555e2833.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/putin-rejects-mobilization-rumors-many-russians-unconvinced/a-79193386?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russia’s President Vladimir Putin has dismissed rumors about military mobilization. But many Russians, including many DW users, say they are preparing for the possibility.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>German economy frets about Saxony-Anhalt election results</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:541469e56faf4ce12179bb75e10aa476f5039ffa5488e63ee468ffd8847a9883</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T18:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-economy-frets-about-saxony-anhalt-election-results/a-79162871--94d137604c23.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-economy-frets-about-saxony-anhalt-election-results/a-79162871?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The AfD won the election in the eastern German state by a wide margin. While politicians and election analysts are still debating the reasons for the far-right party's popularity, economists are sounding the alarm.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ratko Mladic’s funeral casts shadow over Bosnia and Herzegovina vote</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:719197215f2da9e0e67a43f342ccb340215066b2eccb80123bb1df05c713adcd</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T14:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ratko-mladic-s-funeral-casts-shadow-over-bosnia-and-herzegovina-vote/a-79189319--342fd5cbe6c7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ratko-mladic-s-funeral-casts-shadow-over-bosnia-and-herzegovina-vote/a-79189319?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ratko Mladic’s funeral in Belgrade, attended by Serbian and Bosnian Serb leaders, has deepened regional tensions and could affect the upcoming election in Bosnia and Herzegovina.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>BSW and AfD – a political love-hate relationship in Germany</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bb46ad966d0a139c6458081749170a4e17cd13e2030cac28887347698d2af7a7</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T13:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bsw-and-afd-a-political-love-hate-relationship-in-germany/a-79185782--2f6a7962abcf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bsw-and-afd-a-political-love-hate-relationship-in-germany/a-79185782?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Sahra Wagenknecht Alliance (BSW) could help the Alternative for Germany (AfD) into power in Saxony-Anhalt. But the BSW is riddled with infighting</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Afghanistan's women: A national soccer team without a home</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:32163c461c626ac76768b82d6d9c95576fb92b37da655449c37d2d4ddd7ed01c</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T11:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/afghanistan-s-women-a-national-soccer-team-without-a-home/a-79139500--7cfb666b9c3a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/afghanistan-s-women-a-national-soccer-team-without-a-home/a-79139500?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Afghan women's national football team has finally been officially recognized by FIFA. Now the players want to make history both on and off the field.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>PISA 2025 results: Reading and math scores plummet worldwide</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b2115b38c11b2cb2d41230860b6d5291a7a09188b5d9adb5b076353c404822bb</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T07:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pisa-test-reveals-alarming-drop-in-reading-and-math-skills/a-79147293--6fcb0a53f051.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pisa-2025-results-reading-and-math-scores-plummet-worldwide/a-79147293?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The PISA 2025 results reveal record-low student performance, with digital distractions and AI use raising concerns. Germany is faring worse than ever.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Elversberg: Bundesliga newcomers from tiny town make waves</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1a66dd012631c0909e2b0918214032b2dbd5afe6a0a02f3a20b5a528b74eaa6d</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T06:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/elversberg-bundesliga-newcomers-from-tiny-town-make-waves/a-77194483--9d72d35ebb6f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/elversberg-bundesliga-newcomers-from-tiny-town-make-waves/a-77194483?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A team from a small southwestern German town of just 7,000 inhabitants made history by sealing promotion to become the 59th club to play in the Bundesliga. Elversberg has got off to a memorable start.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Female footballers offered egg freezing but doubts remain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:397dd9bba6c29eaf3fc723b0d8782906b59915d0d6f12938bff61b0eaf511fd5</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T06:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/female-footballers-offered-egg-freezing-but-doubts-remain/a-79145259--e96625275f81.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/female-footballers-offered-egg-freezing-but-doubts-remain/a-79145259?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Spain's football federation are set to join a handful of clubs in paying for female players to freeze their eggs during their careers. While players have pushed for the move, there are welfare concerns too.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Werner Herzog: Germany's wild man of cinema is back</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f267f960be171ff835f0650454dda850757ff0c5d1bd7a81befc6ea3edd40583</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T16:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/werner-herzog-germany-s-wild-man-of-cinema-is-back/a-78949324--4a5372e58812.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/werner-herzog-germany-s-wild-man-of-cinema-is-back/a-78949324?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As his latest movie, "Bucking Fastard," premiered at the Venice Film Festival, DW talked to the boundary-breaking director.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Nicaragua challenges German arms exports to Israel at ICJ</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c0912ce7654a433366a603e1b21e466b75d3941b38bce256b765f7eab1a0d397</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T16:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nicaragua-challenges-german-arms-exports-to-israel-at-icj/a-79148044--315737afbbdd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nicaragua-challenges-german-arms-exports-to-israel-at-icj/a-79148044?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany has asked the International Court of Justice to dismiss the case on jurisdiction grounds. It also said its arms exports to Israel were documented, published, and subject to more stringent checks than most.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Saxony-Anhalt: Germany wakes up to 'unsettling' AfD victory</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:897cf9c8a66a382a8ff7692cd48d0b5b1fd6223b19e44b1e3ab9adc619d3c169</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T16:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/saxony-anhalt-germany-wakes-up-to-unsettling-afd-victory/live-78754934--2d9595de9f5f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/saxony-anhalt-germany-wakes-up-to-unsettling-afd-victory/live-78754934?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The far-right Alternative for Germany (AfD) party won the Saxony-Anhalt state election but without an absolute majority in parliament. Other European nations were wrestling with the impact of the results. Follow DW.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>AfD wants to form a government in Saxony-Anhalt — but how?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9ff8ed59a54b399ec601aea715cea5200311de32e63842c88991b1f5f47cb9b8</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T16:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-the-afd-form-a-government-in-saxony-anhalt/a-79107331--72d013c68919.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/afd-wants-to-form-a-government-in-saxony-anhalt-but-how/a-79107331?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Following its record election success, the far-right Alternative for Germany aims to form a government. What options does it have without the absolute majority?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>War criminal Ratko Mladic buried with military honors in Belgrade, Serbia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aaf5c4a2ef0340d441527ad40a65c2ff0d96e0046720053aa236e9cb3aa0ce40</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T15:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/war-criminal-ratko-mladic-buried-with-military-honors-in-belgrade-serbia/a-79148678--c4979d87a1d5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/war-criminal-ratko-mladic-buried-with-military-honors-in-belgrade-serbia/a-79148678?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ratko Mladic, the former Bosnian Serb commander convicted of genocide in Srebrenica, has been buried in Belgrade. The funeral, broadcast live on TV, comes just days before President Vucic is expected to call an election.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Chancellor Merz says AfD result 'changes all of Germany'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:08837fe80c1a7e99e512afae5b5d77de41e086412c970e2e1bef6b6d09fd59db</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T15:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/chancellor-merz-says-afd-result-changes-all-of-germany/a-79150560--fdb0b7e42c28.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/chancellor-merz-says-afd-result-changes-all-of-germany/a-79150560?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A visibly shaken but also determined Friedrich Merz spoke in Berlin about the AfD's election victory in Saxony-Anhalt and the CDU's bitter defeat. He insisted on sticking to his reforms.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>US envoys Witkoff and Kushner hold Ukraine talks after meeting Putin</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:875a09f451a71fbe736831a1c9aa6c530272da97b89add53dd40b917ac37fe69</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T22:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-envoys-witkoff-and-kushner-hold-ukraine-talks-after-meeting-putin/a-79054779--687b66a14041.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-envoys-witkoff-and-kushner-hold-ukraine-talks-after-meeting-putin/a-79054779?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner held talks with Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy in Kyiv, seeking to revive efforts to end the war. But the latest diplomatic push seems to have produced no breakthrough.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Saxony-Anhalt: Digesting the AfD's landmark election win</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4e6840c9c1bb0e84bd9f1a318de6f2bee81013b27fa85d9bcd6b06ee046f4b71</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T21:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/saxony-anhalt-digesting-the-afd-s-landmark-election-win/a-79103981--03f4036eaf84.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/saxony-anhalt-digesting-the-afd-s-landmark-election-win/a-79103981?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">With well over 40% for the far-right Alternative for Germany (AfD), Saxony-Anhalt has witnessed a landmark election night. DW's reporters were on the ground.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Fact check: Election fraud claims spread in Saxony-Anhalt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e1316a7fa4a7262ae93bbef0abf47f49b72e83c140051dfbfa915ea9c22b16cf</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T19:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fact-check-election-fraud-claims-spread-in-saxony-anhalt/a-79093254--984abe33c1c8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fact-check-election-fraud-claims-spread-in-saxony-anhalt/a-79093254?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">False and misleading claims are raising questions about the integrity of the election in Saxony-Anhalt. DW Fact Check takes a closer look.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany set to feel the impact of Saxony-Anhalt's AfD win</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fe7371774a96b652607011fe9b8e6d35fc2390674955349b437d71b735d9859a</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T18:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-set-to-feel-the-impact-of-saxony-anhalt-s-afd-win/a-78874569--97dfb85b6e8e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-set-to-feel-the-impact-of-saxony-anhalt-s-afd-win/a-78874569?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The state election could have major consequences for Germany's government. Pollsters cite dissatisfaction with Merz as one reason for the CDU's poor showing.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Saxony-Anhalt election: Why the AfD is so strong</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bf0e5117819eccde3c6cf678ef52cebe784209d64906838302a2d6868815dc00</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T18:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/saxony-anhalt-election-why-the-afd-is-so-strong/a-78482588--f7f12ed5af71.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/saxony-anhalt-election-why-the-afd-is-so-strong/a-78482588?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The AfD has emerged as the strongest party in Germany's eastern state of Saxony-Anhalt by a wide margin. What is driving support for the far right in this predominantly rural eastern German state?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany, Kosovo unite against ticks carrying deadly virus</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:636202d49e0bedaa4637c2f44920729f32cb0bb9112fef1f14c212d77624d0ce</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T10:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-kosovo-unite-against-ticks-carrying-deadly-virus/a-78655223--2c267f5d11c2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-kosovo-unite-against-ticks-carrying-deadly-virus/a-78655223?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany has high-security labs while Kosovo has Hyalomma ticks and experience with the deadly Crimean-Congo hemorrhagic fever. Working together, German and Kosovar scientists are fighting the disease and its vectors.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany plans anti-drone shield over Leipzig attack — report</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b0af34a8f087f7fc7eda2f27bff12953f2a561dfda6851ee2b358481b634e39d</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T10:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-plans-anti-drone-shield-over-leipzig-attack-report/a-79052604--572615382eed.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-plans-anti-drone-shield-over-leipzig-attack-report/a-79052604?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Several German cities will receive rapidly deployable units capable of defending against drone strikes on critical infrastructure, according to Bild am Sonntag newspaper.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Hungary begins hunt for corrupt regime's billions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3001864a4bcf8379e6df62c7bf359b1d195c39b9d7f5dead0a448b33a638f149</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T05:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hungary-begins-hunt-for-corrupt-regime-s-billions/a-79047176--0dd17c410606.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hungary-begins-hunt-for-corrupt-regime-s-billions/a-79047176?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Hungary's new prime minister promised he would recover billions stolen or diverted by the previous administration. A new "super authority" is about to begin that work. Its success or failure will have a big impact.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Croatia: Toxic waste protest draws tens of thousands</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d890657ac3e2c2d734114d2c493b6d08506c748e2b3b8bace2c0bbdb68a6c9af</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T17:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/croatia-toxic-waste-protest-draws-tens-of-thousands/a-79049228--9dec1bdce80c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/croatia-toxic-waste-protest-draws-tens-of-thousands/a-79049228?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Zagreb demonstrators demanded that the government come up with a plan to clear illegal toxic waste in 20 days. Prime Minister Plenkovic has promised to tackle the issue.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: From emigration to immigration destination</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:37de42eb13ff2f9ef2c68ba41b09026b6b10842cd38821edaf29830b6ffcc07c</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T08:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-from-emigration-to-immigration-destination/a-78805541--ac3bd047b864.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-from-emigration-to-immigration-destination/a-78805541?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Migration is a sensitive topic in Germany, with public debate dominated by the fear of uncontrolled immigration. But over two centuries, millions of Germans emigrated in search of a better life.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Thousands march at Saxony-Anhalt rallies</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e3d812954d08d281ed9d92d5ec6ab92f7ec7178d0eef9d5da910210e0167a2c2</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T06:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-thousands-march-at-saxony-anhalt-rallies/live-79041302--28cda5652dc8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-thousands-march-at-saxony-anhalt-rallies/live-79041302?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ahead of Saxony-Anhalt's state election on Sunday, a democracy festival by civil society groups has been held in Magdeburg. The far-right AfD organized its final campaign rally in the state capital.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>What would an AfD government in Saxony-Anhalt really mean?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:685a044eccf3414c616c9105db3dd5f1e626c48e9b8c7bee272c9b30bb1314bc</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T06:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-would-an-afd-government-in-saxony-anhalt-really-mean/a-78869947--261ff10619b8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-would-an-afd-government-in-saxony-anhalt-really-mean/a-78869947?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Detention centers for deportation, mandatory work for asylum-seekers, vigilante groups — the AfD wants to drastically overhaul Saxony-Anhalt. What does the party have planned?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Outrage as Maltese tycoon acquitted in journalist's murder</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2cdc13d509a2ef7d1fbf9ce5882279a7f4679a6cec16529c535b956446c70325</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T19:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/outrage-as-maltese-tycoon-acquitted-in-journalist-s-murder/a-79027008--2a5e65f2e4f0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/outrage-as-maltese-tycoon-acquitted-in-journalist-s-murder/a-79027008?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Maltese businessman Yorgen Fenech has been found not guilty of complicity to murder journalist Daphne Caruana Galizia. Almost nine years after the attack, the question of who ordered her death remains unanswered.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>In Saxony-Anhalt election, small parties will be kingmakers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2103c98349bcac1a9cc4ee71568a8363d6ed4651922e4c4caea5a54471c1d677</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T19:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/in-saxony-anhalt-election-small-parties-will-be-kingmakers/a-78482460--43a765f0394e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/in-saxony-anhalt-election-small-parties-will-be-kingmakers/a-78482460?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The far-right AfD has good odds of winning an absolute majority in Saxony-Anhalt's parliament this state election, enabling them to govern alone. It all depends on whether other parties make the cut.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's civil society alliance takes on the far right</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:841b8b4fe086df69c5f7904f1a24203ad73c94dd2c39048257e1c42a37a379ef</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T18:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-civil-society-alliance-takes-on-the-far-right/a-79009105--a9caa6e26042.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-civil-society-alliance-takes-on-the-far-right/a-79009105?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Trade unions, churches and human rights activists are worried about the rise of the far-right AfD. How can civil society protect people who are threatened by far-right extremism?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>How vulnerable is Germany's infrastructure?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aa403bf0d746b23a7feb97d2ea16fd36643a93fd2bc7d855f7109bc05eb16c5d</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T13:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-vulnerable-is-germany-s-infrastructure/a-78990131--c453d562d3d7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-vulnerable-is-germany-s-infrastructure/a-78990131?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The growing number of attacks on substations and railway lines in Germany is raising concern. Experts say that people will have to get used to the likelihood that such incidents will continue.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Majority of Germans see Russia as a threat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3215e529ed09e7250e23bd74aee3bbe6cb7b680af3e23ab9f539ab899f1336bc</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T12:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/majority-of-germans-see-russia-as-a-threat/a-78970396--5eab015b811e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/majority-of-germans-see-russia-as-a-threat/a-78970396?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">More than half of German citizens believe that Germany's security is threatened by Russia, according to the latest survey by public broadcaster ARD.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>The hidden environmental cost of AI data centers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fef6864c1f0a05a5dd72da998d06b902feb61765169271ccf7eb4684c09d97a7</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T11:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-hidden-environmental-cost-of-ai-data-centers/a-78789889--5e00024ffa87.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-hidden-environmental-cost-of-ai-data-centers/a-78789889?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As data centers multiply to meet AI demand, they're straining power grids, draining water supplies and reshaping the land and air around them.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Serbia: How the funeral of Ratko Mladic is dividing a nation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1c7ad5c9aedf4c478e7f3d1343573c0a17fb5571d31fc405c371f87fbd86005e</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T11:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/serbia-how-the-funeral-of-ratko-mladic-is-dividing-a-nation/a-78948890--47086bf0a8c5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/serbia-how-the-funeral-of-ratko-mladic-is-dividing-a-nation/a-78948890?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As the Serbian government leaves the decision about Ratko Mladic's funeral arrangements to his family, international pressure on the country is mounting. How do Serbs feel about the matter?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: Is Saxony-Anhalt's economy really struggling?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:872c8b5d00b2883870a4f9e7dcc4c26e02b62b9b132fcaffb805a36066841918</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T10:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-is-saxony-anhalt-s-economy-really-struggling/a-78867143--acfa7a18352e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-is-saxony-anhalt-s-economy-really-struggling/a-78867143?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's far-right AfD party has long claimed that the eastern state of Saxony-Anhalt has been left behind. Is that really the case? A closer look at the data offers some interesting insights.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Why North Korea's women's football team is so good</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:715d6f7258f8df1a8e1f5c3393de46f9d4fb9f39ae0fa3c5e09e526d6d6d52db</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T10:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-north-korea-s-women-s-football-team-is-so-good/a-70313505--6b31ccb5ebf0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-north-korea-s-women-s-football-team-is-so-good/a-70313505?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">North Korea's young footballers enter the U-20 World Cup in Poland as defending champions — the 2024 title was their third. Why is the isolated state so good at the game?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>2026 Beethoven Festival evokes a sense of home</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1de6fb61cd63bbb001a1a813f88a36100ca9afee5ed7d77fc598ac45fc183651</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T08:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/2026-beethoven-festival-evokes-a-sense-of-home/a-78892997--9bbbc99c220c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/2026-beethoven-festival-evokes-a-sense-of-home/a-78892997?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The motto of this year's classical music festival in Bonn is "Home/At Home," featuring musicians from diverse cultures presenting pieces from their homelands.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>How Volkswagen's huge workforce became a costly burden</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:73f7d61a4b4b55d28b564087441cf8a198e7e0fbaf8cc09ee7282098f4bedd82</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T07:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-volkswagen-s-huge-workforce-became-a-costly-burden/a-77766154--6b1e762393dc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-volkswagen-s-huge-workforce-became-a-costly-burden/a-77766154?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The struggling German carmaker plans to cut up to 100,000 jobs from its 630,000-strong workforce. How did VW's headcount get so bloated, and will the cuts be enough to survive the Chinese EV onslaught?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Berlin: BER Airport Terminal 1 reopened after security scare</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1b5747d8d5f71b285b072c6ee7abdeda2421f3d184b104af0343958d174fd9e6</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T21:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/berlin-ber-airport-terminal-1-evacuated-after-security-scare/a-78895207--c34e813b5301.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/berlin-ber-airport-terminal-1-reopened-after-security-scare/a-78895207?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Police have given the all-clear at Terminal 1 at Berlin's BER Airport following an earlier security scare and evacuation. The airport said some flights had been delayed but they were trying to avoid any cancelations.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Norway seizes Russian ship in Svalbard to compensate Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4dd3e3137d2550980ff5bda746d20681d8644f555c55dd6c5f49b010eb7faff4</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T15:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/norway-seizes-russian-ship-in-svalbard-to-compensate-ukraine/a-78889005--08f506bc071c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/norway-seizes-russian-ship-in-svalbard-to-compensate-ukraine/a-78889005?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Authorities in Norway have seized a Russian ship, the Professor Molchanov, on a court order sought and obtained by Naftogaz in Ukraine. Russia has protested the move, which stems from its refusal to pay Naftogaz damages.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Is Germany's economic slump finally over?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:060e39ed183dae8384b7793e16f732fe0f84dc25e3c5d43bae56ecbdab26238c</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T12:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-germany-s-economic-slump-finally-over/a-78815447--a101d614d4d2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-germany-s-economic-slump-finally-over/a-78815447?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Despite a slew of negative headlines, the German economy has posted its best figures in years. There are reasons for optimism, but structural issues remain.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Macron visits Bayeux Tapestry with King Charles, PM Andy Burnham</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8144c3fa4925684f6f85c2533443676191e09fa225ac6cfb9dd6bd8847e1b0e6</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T16:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/macron-visits-bayeux-tapestry-with-king-charles-pm-andy-burnham/a-78772317--2945f5b2dad4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/macron-visits-bayeux-tapestry-with-king-charles-pm-andy-burnham/a-78772317?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron is on a shorter-term visit to the UK than the renowned on-loan 11th century tapestry. He viewed the ancient artwork with the UK monarch and relatively new Prime Minister Andy Burnham.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Austria women ice hockey team fight for future generations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0619cad458eeede17189c12ae722d19cb813295bfbfd87a972f178341de86d13</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T15:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/austria-women-ice-hockey-team-fight-for-future-generations/a-78771578--3801f62b822d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/austria-women-ice-hockey-team-fight-for-future-generations/a-78771578?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Austria are getting ready for their first Women's Ice Hockey World Championship. But preparations have been overshadowed by a dispute about conditions, pay and getting men's cast-off kit. A solution now looks in sight.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>EU summons Russian envoy over failed Leipzig drone attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6b3e8653a2cb6aa95edebcb027a3fc6b7307385c07fc0587ee53d1b29b29e027</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T08:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-summons-russian-envoy-over-failed-leipzig-drone-attack/a-78687280--4f4b3de05209.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-summons-russian-envoy-over-failed-leipzig-drone-attack/a-78687280?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU's foreign policy chief Kaja Kallas said the attempted attack had "all the hallmarks of state-sponsored terrorism." She said the EU was summoning a Russian envoy, with France announcing a similar step.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Women's football: Anyomi, London City and the German exodus</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:106796ee7d25e6a1a9397b459c541b478cf332854fc6aaa690ba6d6ec43b2358</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T07:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/women-s-football-anyomi-london-city-and-the-german-exodus/a-78446131--1f6d62473b8a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/women-s-football-anyomi-london-city-and-the-german-exodus/a-78446131?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nicole Anyomi has joined Alexia Putellas and other star names in signing for the ambitious English club London City Lionesses. The Germany winger told DW England is a better place to develop her game than back home.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: Russia threatens 'devastating' Baltic response</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:45df56530bff6aab550ff62832f149e45f7ae15370a4308b840fbf549527ac4a</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T00:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-russia-threatens-devastating-baltic-response/live-78582421--a061a45930f9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-russia-threatens-devastating-baltic-response/live-78582421?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Any escalation in the Baltic region will lead to a significant response, Moscow said.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany says Russia behind attempted drone attack at Leipzig airport</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8da29d92c8ecc0928289abf6044a5023e400a50096650463eec511a4682c3586</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T22:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-says-russia-behind-attempted-drone-attack-at-leipzig-airport/a-78584589--1b81c9b87e46.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-says-russia-behind-attempted-drone-attack-at-leipzig-airport/a-78584589?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Investigators believe an explosives-laden drone was deliberately targeting a Ukrainian cargo aircraft at Leipzig/Halle airport in early August. The German government said on Tuesday that it held Russia "responsible."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Can communities be protected from melting glaciers?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f3408c1c4502dd036b12c1f33a9ed53fbd009d861d77a1f1c783b93e5c7ffb72</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T13:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/as-glaciers-melt-can-communities-be-protected/a-78615775--a898d3259825.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-communities-be-protected-from-melting-glaciers/a-78615775?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Rising temperatures are increasing the risk of floods and avalanches in mountain regions. The disaster in Nepal and Tibet shows the urgent need for solutions, and the tools that could help save lives.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Mladic's death, Bosnia and Serbia's unfinished reckoning</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b507609ce13eb9cc88176d6e1fd5fe649890feeb11c9f71c58fc3f1b7ab57dec</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T13:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/mladic-s-death-bosnia-and-serbia-s-unfinished-reckoning/a-78602733--165fe4759bb5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/mladic-s-death-bosnia-and-serbia-s-unfinished-reckoning/a-78602733?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The death of Ratko Mladic did not close a dark chapter of European history; it reopened old wounds. The ideology that created him lives on. The Dayton peace agreement ended the war, not the divisions that produced it.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Norway's new King Haakon VIII takes oath in parliament</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:46460fb5829ab6a194da34e08449ead1053bdf6427f6db60b1adc87876a4b160</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T12:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/norway-s-new-king-haakon-viii-takes-oath-in-parliament/a-78606923--f49dd1cbb150.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/norway-s-new-king-haakon-viii-takes-oath-in-parliament/a-78606923?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The new king swore to uphold the constitution in parliament in Oslo, the first major institutional step of his reign. Haakon VIII's wife Queen Mette-Marit had to skip the event in the aftermath of her lung transplant.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US irks Germany, Europe with Russian G20 invite, press bans</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:925ae3325865dccdc066345d423a2b16943a14e5549ac5d973362d1ef19eb63d</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T10:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-irks-germany-europe-with-russian-g20-invite-press-bans/a-78583919--4573442379c3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-irks-germany-europe-with-russian-g20-invite-press-bans/a-78583919?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russia's finance minister is at the G20 meeting in Asheville but some key US press corps members are not. The mood was already tense amid the lengthy Iran war and Trump's renewed beef with neighbor Canada.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Can new Apple CEO John Ternus fix the tech giant's AI woes?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5fe1ba89416464a3c8a5fee6a96138a03a77bdacf3e3ecf8159efc2a3c84e152</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T09:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-new-apple-ceo-john-ternus-fix-the-tech-giant-s-ai-woes/a-78575898--ec9f6d3fb1f9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-new-apple-ceo-john-ternus-fix-the-tech-giant-s-ai-woes/a-78575898?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">John Ternus is just the third Apple CEO in 30 years. His primary challenge is to correct the company's faltering AI strategy to preserve its position as a big tech leader.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>At Venice Film Festival, politics take center stage</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3b2c38a7f403256d937c936e55bfd6261524f3050b781401cc31f72257a315cd</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T14:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/at-venice-film-festival-politics-take-center-stage/a-78493761--39adfe1f0702.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/at-venice-film-festival-politics-take-center-stage/a-78493761?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">With works about Gaza, Ukraine and Elon Musk, political cinema is in the spotlight at the 2026 Venice Film Festival.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Canada's Carney holds firm against Trump tariffs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ab3dec435c782dffaaadc6b20a89f5d0253fb8e149f04ac3038af37578a386f4</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T13:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/canada-s-carney-holds-firm-against-trump-tariffs/a-78542754--4ad6d16c6985.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/canada-s-carney-holds-firm-against-trump-tariffs/a-78542754?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Canada is facing new US import penalties after Prime Minister Mark Carney refused to match US tariffs on China. Other countries are watching as the Trump trade clash turns into a fight over economic sovereignty.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Inside the sea cucumber smuggling boom</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:324f0d971671a0d4358c4611b540b98a796387acf894ae3a3fe69b7a188a5f53</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T10:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/inside-the-sea-cucumber-smuggling-boom/a-78005662--ad829420fb34.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/inside-the-sea-cucumber-smuggling-boom/a-78005662?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A quiet multimillion‑dollar black market is exploding across the Indian Ocean, driven by one unlikely animal: the sea cucumber.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Ailing Djokovic 'despised' every moment of US Open defeat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ffba8d841f61d58a2b66fa9d2d28f6a91344f8fae5ba4dbf5dcfb33eb9ba77a1</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T09:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ailing-djokovic-despised-every-moment-of-us-open-defeat/a-78572187--352c93994800.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ailing-djokovic-despised-every-moment-of-us-open-defeat/a-78572187?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Novak Djokovic has exited in the first round of a Grand Slam for the first time in over two decades. Could time — or an unknown health condition — be catching up with the Serbian tennis legend?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>EU wants drones to spray pesticides, but it could backfire</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7fc9548ff55a8484c2094c617d5311d197e114a0e1f895568ab44246ecb68dbb</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T15:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-wants-drones-to-spray-pesticides-but-it-could-backfire/a-78557154--b8aa3ba6b326.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-wants-drones-to-spray-pesticides-but-it-could-backfire/a-78557154?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU wants to lift a decades-old ban on spraying pesticides from the air, allowing drones to be used for greater precision. But experts warn the plan could lead to even more pesticides being used in agriculture.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Greece, Turkey clash over protected Aegean marine areas</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:96483ef5330a65520d197b61b63ebb718bab330b776cc939318c8bb29f78f54f</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T09:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/greece-turkey-clash-over-protected-aegean-marine-areas/a-78550021--ccf9d418d0a0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/greece-turkey-clash-over-protected-aegean-marine-areas/a-78550021?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Turkey has announced the creation of two protected zones in a disputed area of the Aegean Sea, sparking an angry reaction from Greece. Does this mark a new chapter in a long-running dispute between the two countries?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Russian-American heads Trump's planned Caucasus trade route</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8ed20b5624d059c9d268431b6afddbea4f12745dc564e2cb2ac0674dd5258251</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T16:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russian-american-heads-trump-s-planned-caucasus-trade-route/a-78547064--b0ca155f3d56.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russian-american-heads-trump-s-planned-caucasus-trade-route/a-78547064?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Russian-born businessman heads the investment fund financing the so-called "Trump Route," a planned corridor through Armenia linking Azerbaijan with Nakhchivan. Who is Konstantin Sokolov, and what role does he play?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>This extremely successful author polarizes German readers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:965f8afb050fe3a052954d20be25e6b6e7b3c1a33d119f7ac220bef9fde1e79f</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T07:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/this-extremely-successful-author-polarizes-german-readers/a-78500452--1ca180b39c00.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/this-extremely-successful-author-polarizes-german-readers/a-78500452?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">She's young and she says what she thinks: Caroline Wahl is topping Germany's bestseller lists with her novels. But she has also faced a public backlash.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Serbia keeps EU, Russia in play ahead of key election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f2a725e60175a0d3fd72576fcb4c8c3bde1cba187090d0cc03db0db39cdc6ef8</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T07:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/serbia-keeps-eu-russia-in-play-ahead-of-key-election/a-78543495--328f068dfd52.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/serbia-keeps-eu-russia-in-play-ahead-of-key-election/a-78543495?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Serbia heads toward an uncertain election, President Aleksandar Vucic is balancing ties with Russia and EU ambitions. But growing geopolitical tensions and pressure at home are narrowing his room to maneuver.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>What 'The Odyssey' can teach us about climate chaos</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6a854814ea7d83b7511e8864f8880737aa446cb278e68248cb2f594a48eb5489</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T12:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-the-odyssey-can-teach-us-about-climate-chaos/a-78545407--d5adc3479f14.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-the-odyssey-can-teach-us-about-climate-chaos/a-78545407?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Bronze Age collapse may have started with a water crisis. The droughts of today raise the unsettling question of whether it could happen again.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Influential humanists: These are the winners of the Goethe Medal 2026</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1780b337c606ef40a09545195e3074d853388e2c18b53b9be9bc6062467d3ad8</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T12:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/influential-humanists-these-are-the-winners-of-the-goethe-medal-2026/a-78497975--2a003f94b40a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/influential-humanists-these-are-the-winners-of-the-goethe-medal-2026/a-78497975?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The prestigious German cultural award recognizes the artistic work and commitment to cultural dialogue of Arvo Pärt, Anita Raja and Prodromos Tsinikoris.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's military wants to recruit tech-savvy gamers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1868aa9be3c34c82ca316049878b27047ed85659cff03a803998ad1b2f0940af</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T10:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-military-wants-to-recruit-tech-savvy-gamers/a-78536462--a4ab0409cda1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-military-wants-to-recruit-tech-savvy-gamers/a-78536462?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Bundeswehr has been a fixture at Gamescom, Cologne's video game trade fair, for years. But critics say military recruitment does not belong at an entertainment convention.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Norway's King Harald dies at 89</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dd9fbfd6f8c5065e8725e161466d066d232bc1b0c413d69f57375d1fc3b0c29f</id><updated>2026-09-10T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T08:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/norway-s-king-harald-dies-at-89/a-78524572--172e0c27118c.html" type="text/html" /><link re